From 700ef2f619c84241efd363115badb4b83298debf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:39:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/26] validation: strict server-side charset rules for values
 that reach build scripts

The generator workflows paste appname, compname, server, key, apiServer,
urlLink, downloadLink and androidappid into bash/pwsh/sed/perl with
${{ env.X }}. Since #303 only appname/compname were filtered, and only
against a denylist; server, key and the URLs could inject into sed or the
shell of the runner, which holds the signing secrets.

- New rdgenerator/validation.py with allowlist regexes per field (host
  names/IPs, 44-char base64 key, http(s) URLs without query strings, Java
  package ids, names limited to letters, digits, space and . _ ( ) + , -).
  The form (clean()) and the JSON API share it. The workflow decrypt step
  re-checks the same rules (added in a later commit).
- serverPort must be between 1 and 65532, because relay and websocket
  ports are derived as +1..+3.
- Default/override option names must be simple identifiers. The
  permanent password and the manual settings text are length-capped.
- sanitize_filename(): upstream's r'[^\w\s-]' let tabs and newlines
  through into ${{ env.filename }}. Now only [A-Za-z0-9_-] is allowed.
- PNG uploads are capped at 4 MB. Logo and privacy uploads are checked
  too, not only the icon.
- The generator page shows every field error, not just icon errors.
- API: an omitted boolean now takes the web form's default. Upstream
  defaulted all 20 booleans to False (keyboard, clipboard, ... off),
  unlike the UI. Non-string values are rejected instead of crashing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
